  "title": "Keep the MLP Nonlinearity Local",
  "introduction": "Let $X$ be shared token representations, and column-partition the first MLP weight as $A=[A_1,A_2]$. Worker $i$ can form $Y_i=\\operatorname{GeLU}(XA_i)$ without communicating because its output-feature partition is complete. A row-partitioned second weight then consumes the matching $Y_i$ locally; only the resulting partial outputs must be summed.",
